text:
Nia R: Quick repro: sampleapp produced duplicate side-effects when a 429 hit just as OIDC refresh finished. Short log dump below.

Nia R: Steps to reproduce:
1) client sends job J (medium payload)
2) server replies 429
3) SDK backoff fires a retry quickly
4) auth refresh completes and the original logical op is re-emitted -> server processes twice (no stable op id)

Carlos M: Do we currently emit any operation-scoped id out of the box? I thought only some examples added headers manually.

Ethan B: Nope, not by default. That's the parity sink. Node sample had a manual header but other SDKs lack it.

Nia R: Proposal: add a small middleware called "SafeBackoff" into sdk-core. Responsibilities: generate a short replay token header `Replay-Token`, persist it across retries/refresh cycles, and mark streams as non-replayable unless user opts in.

Carlos M: Nice. Also add a refresh-aware gate: if a token refresh is in-flight, the middleware should bias the next retry delay by +refreshEstimateMs and decrement a per-op fast-retry budget so we don't do multiple immediate retries while refresh is happening. Default fast-retry budget = 1.

Ethan B: Jitter idea: percentile jitter based on payload size distribution. Compute payload_percentile = clamp(payload_kb / 100, 0.01, 0.9). jitter_ms = baseMs * (1 + payload_percentile) * uniform(0.6..1.4). This keeps tiny payloads low-latency but scales smoothly for larger ones. Different from sqrt/ln proposals.

Nia R: I like percentile approach; it's easy to explain in docs. We'll expose a hook so teams can swap in ln/sqrt formulas if they prefer. Default baseMs = 60ms.

Carlos M: Telemetry: emit events `safe_backoff.token_created`, `safe_backoff.retry_delayed_for_refresh`, `safe_backoff.replay_attempted`, `safe_backoff.server_deduped`. These help see server-side adoption.

Ethan B: For sampleapp onboarding, add `conservativePlayback: true` option that turns on SafeBackoff, marks streaming as not replayable, and prints server dedupe snippet. Example server snippet: 
```
const seen = new Map();
app.post('/v1/generate', (req, res) => {
  const token = req.header('Replay-Token');
  if (token && seen.has(token)) return res.status(200).json({duplicate: true});
  if (token) seen.set(token, Date.now());
  // process request
});
// server TTL guidance: min(max(1s, procMs * 2), 30s)
```

Nia R: Edgecases: if server ignores header, SafeBackoff still reduces duplicates via refresh gating + strict fast-retry budget. Also require explicit opt-in for production clients until servers widely honor Replay-Token.

safeplay-bot: (automated) Created ticket DEVTICKET-901: "SafeBackoff middleware: Replay-Token, refresh-aware delay, percentile-jitter, fast-retry budget, streaming non-replayable, sampleapp conservative mode"

Carlos M: I'll prototype Go behavior mapping for auth refresh state. Ethan can take Node + sampleapp patch. Nia will produce the spec and tests.

Ethan B: I'll add a small e2e that simulates 429 + refresh = 320ms and asserts server saw one unique token when Replay-Token is set. Also include a test asserting streaming ops are skipped from replay.

Nia R: Thanks all. Adding to SDK sync agenda and linking DEVTICKET-901. :calendar:
